\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

\looseness=-2 We presented an adaptive inference-time compute pipeline for frozen flow-matching VLAs. The $K{=}2$ $L_2$ probe ($\rho{=}0.9979$) gates selective CRM correction, achieving $18.3$\% Object / $35.0$\% Spatial ($+$7.3 / $+$5.7\,pp vs.\ VLA-only) while matching or exceeding fixed-$K{=}10$ unconditional correction with 80\% fewer VLA forward passes. On fixed-$K$ analysis baselines, learned correction contributes 55--78\% of the gain.
\textbf{Limitations.}\enspace All experiments use LIBERO in simulation with SmolVLA (450M); real-robot transfer and larger VLAs ($\pi_0$) are untested. Absolute success rates are far from deployment-ready. The CRM requires task-specific calibration ($-$12\,pp on unseen tasks). The pipeline requires stochastic sample diversity, excluding tokenized VLAs (Appendix~\ref{sec:applicability}); whether the $K{=}2$ probe generalizes to diffusion-based VLAs is open. AI tools assisted with code and manuscript.

